#! clause: E5.4
#! mode: run
#! requires: each, read_line
#! expect-fault: nested-suspend
# R4 / forbid-and-fault (D-M7-1, S-15): a suspending capability reached inside a FOREIGN
# block-consumer's reentrant drive is a terminal `NestedSuspend` fault. `each` drives its block on
# the host stack, so the block's `read_line()` cannot suspend-and-resume through it — the engine
# faults deterministically rather than freezing native progress. The idiom is inversion, not
# suspend-the-outer-drive (see the parity control `reentry-002`). No `input:` — it never resolves.
each([1]) do (x)
  print(read_line())
end
